## Task

Extract from the act:

- its official title and the citation of the publication;
- the date of the act (Ausfertigungsdatum), not the date of publication;
- every article, and for each one which law it changes and whether it amends, creates or repeals;
- the entry-into-force rules, article by article. Many acts contain several: a fixed date for some
  articles, "am Tag nach der Verkündung" for others. Copy a rule as `rule_text` when it is not a
  fixed date — never convert it into a date yourself;
- two or three neutral sentences in German saying what the act does.

Abbreviations of target laws (AufenthG, EStG, SGB II …) are taken from the text; do not guess one
that is not written there. If an article changes a law whose title you cannot read from the input,
leave the target fields empty and note it in the summary.

Answer with JSON matching the schema. No text around it.
